{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973388-abyssal-the-suffering","id":973388,"title":"Abyssal: the Suffering","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-20T14:28:50-07:00","id":973388,"title":"Abyssal: the Suffering","content":"What are the rules for mortals with a soul made of the Abyss? I been thinking of an Abyssal splat for some time now. They would actually be like regular mortals, but anyone who can see into other's souls/spirits/aura would be extremely unsettled (especially Mages). I haven't figured out yet what would be their power stat, integrity equivalent, yadda yadda yadda, ect.. One of the themes is Innocence/Suffering with a heavy dose of I am scared/I like new me. Their powers could even involve screwing around with the powers/abilities/gadgets of the other splats cuz you know the Abyss is Unreality and mucks about with casuality and possibility (I think). If I am wrong, please correct me. Also I am thinking that the good guys (Wardens) are those that seek to restrain the advance of the Abyssals have a hard-on for chaos, evil doing, blah blah blah. There are several other kind of groupings, but I will post them later. So what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:56:53-07:00","id":973408,"title":"","content":"There are a couple of beings detailed in Intruders and I think Night Horrors: Unbidden. Probably the best bet is the Abyssal Nativity. It can be a pretty compelling idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their powers could even involve screwing around with the powers/abilities/gadgets of the other splats cuz you know the Abyss is Unreality and mucks about with casuality and possibility (I think). </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. The issue with giving them distinct powers aside from messing with paradox is that the Abyss defies catagorisation. It does everything and nothing at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:16:05-07:00","id":973427,"title":"","content":"It has potential, though I wonder if it would share too much head space with Mage. There are already Scelestus that pretty much have their soul replaced with an Abyssal verge (qlipoth is memory serves). I would also have to ask how these people aren't purely antagonists, you're using the abyss from Mage which you yourself mention is a source of literal unreality, combine this with the way it corrupts and befouls, I have a hard time seeing how the abyss or mortals empowered by it could be protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 09-20-2016, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:25:59-07:00","id":973477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973388-abyssal-the-suffering?p=973427#post973427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are already Scelestus that pretty much have their soul replaced with an Abyssal verge (qlipoth is memory serves).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Qlipoth are pospective archmasters who were lost to the Abyss and then hollowed out and returned to the Fallen World. It's not really the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also have to ask how these people aren't purely antagonists, you're using the abyss from Mage which you yourself mention is a source of literal unreality, combine this with the way it corrupts and befouls, I have a hard time seeing how the abyss or mortals empowered by it could be protagonists. </div> </div> </div>Well, they're still human. The versions present in Mage already tend to revolve around that dicotomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","